1. Write a query that returns a list of all product prices such that the result should look like this -
+--------------+--------------+-------------+
| ProductName  | PriceType    | PriceValue  |
+--------------+--------------+-------------+
| Product A    | Sale Price   | 119.99      |
| Product A    | List Price   | 150.00      |
| Product B    | Sale Price   | 24.99       |
| Product B    | List Price   | 29.99       |
+--------------+--------------+-------------+

2. How do you pivot the above results such that the result view looks flat (like below)?
+--------------+-------------+-------------+
| ProductName  | SalePrice   | ListPrice   |
+--------------+-------------+-------------+
| Product A    | 119.99      | 150.00      |
| Product B    | 24.55       | 29.99       |
+--------------+-------------+-------------+

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. SELECT pp.ProductName, pt.Name AS PriceType, pp.PriceValue FROM tblProductPrice pp JOIN tblPriceType pt ON pp.PriceTypeId = pt.Id order by ProductName;

2. 
SELECT ProductName,
  CASE WHEN PriceType = 'Sale Price' THEN PriceValue END AS SalePrice,
  CASE WHEN PriceType = 'List Price' THEN PriceValue END AS ListPrice
FROM (
  SELECT pp.ProductName, pt.Name AS PriceType, pp.PriceValue FROM tblProductPrice pp JOIN tblPriceType pt ON pp.PriceTypeId = pt.Id
) AS Source order by ProductName;

SELECT ProductName,
  MAX(CASE WHEN PriceType = 'Sale Price' THEN PriceValue END) AS SalePrice,
  MAX(CASE WHEN PriceType = 'List Price' THEN PriceValue END) AS ListPrice
FROM (
  SELECT pp.ProductName, pt.Name AS PriceType, pp.PriceValue FROM tblProductPrice pp JOIN tblPriceType pt ON pp.PriceTypeId = pt.Id
) AS Source
GROUP BY ProductName order by ProductName;

